# 品味宪法 / Taste Constitution (product sense + marketing instinct)

Shared across all agents (Claude Code, Codex, OMP, Hermes). 这是 `RULES.md "Judgment principles"`
的完整正文，只在**产品/营销任务**触发时展开细读。工程任务不读本文件。

本文件是 `lessons.md` 的品味姊妹：`lessons.md` 积累工程教训，`taste-log.md` 积累
**人对"什么叫做好"的判断**。宪法是积累的**产物**，不是起点——规则由 `taste-log.md`
里反复出现的真人裁决晋升上来（同一规则出现 ≥3 次，且至少一条为 `observed-buyer` / `measured`，见 §0 来源门）。

维护说明：本文件唯一真相源。Codex/Claude 在运行时通过 harness 规则指针读取本文件；
改动后按 `runtime-setup.md` 跑 `runtime-install.py verify`（旧的 `~/.codex/rules-snapshot.py` 快照已不再使用）。
硬上限：**禁令 6 条、评分维度 5 个**。超过即视为退化。

---

## 0. 何时生效 / When this binds + 校准范围

**触发词**（命中任一即展开本文件，并 grep `<harness>/taste-log.md`）：
该不该做 / 值不值得 / 要不要开发 / 这个功能 / MVP / wedge / 砍需求 / 产品方向 /
定价 / pricing / margin / landing / 文案 / copy / hook / 标题 / offer / 套餐 /
# 网站开发：响应式、移动端实用验收与复发学习

版本：1.3.0（2026-10-21 新增 §0 默认要求；2026-10-22 品位禁令改为 FAIL，Jobs review 铁律）。用户明确要求：2026-10-14，网站要重视响应式和移动端体验，降低理解与操作负担；agent 要实际打开使用，主动发现、解决问题，并对重复问题学习和预防。

适用：新建网站、修改网站 UI、修复网站问题。以本文件所在的 active harness 为来源，项目既有规则和当前任务授权共同限定范围。本文件定义当前网站体验验收；`ui-build-doctrine.md` 保留已有布局循环细节，`computer-use-acceptance.md` 提供通用启动、取证与有界修复流程。只更新规则文件时做规则加载验证，不据此声称某个网站体验通过。

## 0. Default requirements, even when unasked

User direction (2026-10-21): "很多时候没提移动端网页，agent 就默认只优化 PC 端网页，这是不对的要响应式的，
移动端的体验，交互，界面，速度等等，SEO 等等都十分重要，这些都是默认的要求". A request to build or change a
website that never mentions phones, speed or SEO still requires all of the following. Only the
user's own words waive one (for example "desktop-only admin tool"); "not requested" is not a
waiver. The list is `routes/web-defaults.md`; the `web` module of `core/policy.json` points every
agent to it without the user naming a site (`context_modules`, docs/adr/0034): on each session whose
directory is a web project (an `index.html`, or a front-end framework in `package.json`), at the first
edit of a front-end file (`.tsx`, `.vue`, `.css`, `.html` ...; harness and temp-folder report pages
excepted), and on prompts that name a site, a page, its UI or its users' experience.

**Steal, then let the user choose** (user, 2026-10-29: "我现在发现 agent 给我建网站，自己瞎搞，good artists copy great
artist steal，要找对标，然后给我几个让我选，效果要部署到线上，有时候我是手机上远程的，不在电脑旁边"). A new site, a redesign or a
Website defaults (user requirement, 2026-10-21; website-experience.md §0). They apply even when the request never mentions phones, speed or SEO. A request that says nothing about mobile still means a responsive site; only the user can waive one, by saying so (for example "desktop-only admin tool").
- Steal, then let the user choose (user, 2026-10-29: "good artists copy great artist steal，要找对标，然后给我几个让我选，效果要部署到线上，有时候我是手机上远程的"): a new site or a new look is never improvised. Before building it, find the best sites for the same job (at least two, captured), build 2 to 4 options that each steal look, layout and interaction from a named benchmark (never their words, images or brand), deploy each to a public link and send one phone page to choose from: `python <harness>/scripts/design_options.py --spec options.json` (website-experience.md §0 "Steal, then let the user choose"). Until the user picks, build only what no option changes (data, backend, SEO, the core flow's logic). A fix or small change inside a chosen look needs none of this.
- Value first (user, 2026-10-28): a site exists to give its buyer clearly more value than the price, and the buyer must see it without reading: real outputs, the product in use and the scenario as pictures, little text. Sell the buyer's result, not the mechanism. Value questions differ by stage (before building, while building, before launch, after launch); ask them again at every stage and write the current answers down (website-experience.md §0 "Value first").
- Mobile-first, responsive: build and check 375 px first, then tablet and desktop. Use a viewport meta tag, fluid layout, no sideways scrolling, and images and tables that fit a phone.
- Touch: targets of 44 px (never under 24 px), no action that needs hover, inputs at 16 px or more with the right type and autocomplete, and nothing fixed that covers the content or the main button.
- Phone interface: 16 px body text, one clear main action per screen, navigation that works with one thumb, and visible loading, error and success states.
- Speed on a mid-range phone over 4G: LCP 2.5 s or less, CLS 0.1 or less, little JavaScript, images sized and compressed, below-the-fold images lazy-loaded.
- SEO: a unique title and meta description, one H1, `lang`, canonical, Open Graph tags, structured data where it fits, robots.txt and a sitemap, and pages left indexable.
- Taste (the user's design bar; read website-experience.md §0 Taste before UI work): show the product working and its result instead of describing it, with a tool's action in the hero; a stranger understands it in 5 seconds; subtract before adding; readable text, never faint, translucent or gradient-filled; one design system, no template look (repeated heading + three cards, glow, emoji icons); web-check FAILs text under WCAG AA contrast, gradient text and emoji icons, so fix the colour token or component instead of reporting them.
- Components (user requirement, 2026-10-28): when the user names no component library and the project has no design system of its own, use shadcn/ui for ordinary UI and Magic UI on landing pages, with AI SDK Elements for AI input and output and Lucide icons; do not hand-roll equivalents (website-experience.md §0 "Named components").
- One language per page (user requirement, 2026-10-28: "网页要注意不要多语言夹杂"): every visible string, placeholder, aria-label, alt text, toast, empty state, title and description is in the page's language, and `<html lang>` matches it; translate component-library defaults ("Submit", "Search...", "No results"). Exempt: brand and product names, acronyms, code, and a language switcher's own labels. A multilingual site keeps each locale clean. web-check FAILs `taste/mixed-language`.
- Core task (user requirement, 2026-10-28: "用户核心使用步骤要非常短，核心操作也必须在一个页面完成，就连下滑也不用就可以完成核心功能操作"): the fewest possible steps, all on one page, and at 375x812 the core action starts and finishes in the first screen with no scrolling (input, main button and result visible together). web-check FAILs `core-flow/above-the-fold` when no field or call to action sits in the first phone screen, or a form begun there submits from below it.
- Guide at the moment of need (user, 2026-10-31: "就算我不说，也要自动给我…让用户在我的产品使用过程中没有障碍"): unasked, list every shortcut, gesture and hidden feature, and teach each with an in-product hint when the user's own input shows the need (the slow way, a near miss, a mistake, a stall), never on load: one at a time, dismissible, at most once per page and three times in all, gone once used; touch gesture on phones, key on desktop. A core task needing a hint is a defect to fix. Prove each trigger by real use (website-experience.md §0).
- SEO and GEO (2026-10-28): besides the SEO items above, write for answer engines: content in the served HTML, not only after JavaScript runs (most AI crawlers run none); robots.txt lets search and AI crawlers in (GPTBot, OAI-SearchBot, ClaudeBot, PerplexityBot, Google-Extended); an `/llms.txt`; pages that answer the buyer's question in plain, quotable sentences. web-check FAILs `geo/server-rendered` and `geo/ai-crawlers`, WARNs a missing llms.txt. Writing citable pages: skill `geo-page`.
- Usable by agents and accessible (2026-10-28): agents act through the accessibility tree, so the same rules serve both. Every control has an accessible name and a real `<button>`, `<a>` or form element (no clickable divs); visible labels on fields; a `<main>` landmark; full keyboard use with a visible focus ring; `prefers-reduced-motion` stops endless animation (Magic UI included); the core task reachable by a stable URL or a plain form. web-check FAILs unnamed controls and WARNs the rest.

